The statements (as Lean prints them):
@Pnq.gBeyond : {p q n : ℕ} → Pnq.Tree p q n → ℕ → Finset ℕ
@Pnq.balanced_base : ∀ {p q : ℕ},
  2 ≤ p →
    2 ≤ q →
      p.Coprime q →
        ∀ {n : ℕ} (t : Pnq.Tree p q n) (a0 : ℕ),
          Pnq.F t 0 →
            (∀ (ℓ : ℕ), 1 ≤ ℓ → ℓ < a0 → Pnq.F t ℓ) →
              1 ≤ a0 → a0 ≤ n → ¬Pnq.F t a0 → q * p ^ (Pnq.e t + (Pnq.gBeyond t a0).card) ≤ Pnq.size t
@Pnq.balanced_plus : ∀ {p q : ℕ},
  2 ≤ p →
    2 ≤ q →
      p.Coprime q →
        ∀ {n : ℕ} (t : Pnq.Tree p q n) (a0 : ℕ),
          Pnq.F t 0 →
            (∀ (ℓ : ℕ), 1 ≤ ℓ → ℓ < a0 → Pnq.F t ℓ) →
              1 ≤ a0 →
                a0 ≤ n →
                  ¬Pnq.F t a0 →
                    (Pnq.gBeyond t a0).Nonempty →
                      (∀ ℓ < a0, ¬Pnq.E t ℓ) →
                        (¬Pnq.E t a0 ∨
                            p = 2 ∧ ∀ (b : ℕ), a0 < b → (∀ g ∈ Pnq.gBeyond t a0, b < g) → Pnq.E t b → Pnq.F t b) →
                          q * p ^ Pnq.e t * (p ^ (Pnq.gBeyond t a0).card + 1) ≤ Pnq.size t
@Pnq.levelsBeyond : {p q n : ℕ} → [Fact (Nat.Prime p)] → [Fact (Nat.Prime q)] → Finset (ZMod (p ^ n * q)) → ℕ → Finset ℕ
Pnq.balanced_base_zmod : ∀ (p q n : ℕ) [inst : Fact (Nat.Prime p)] [inst_1 : Fact (Nat.Prime q)],
  p ≠ q →
    ∀ (A : Finset (ZMod (p ^ n * q))) (a0 : ℕ),
      Pqr.ZeroAt A q →
        (∀ (ℓ : ℕ), 1 ≤ ℓ → ℓ < a0 → Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ ℓ * q)) →
          1 ≤ a0 →
            a0 ≤ n → ¬Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ a0 * q) → q * p ^ ((Pnq.levelsE A).card + (Pnq.levelsBeyond A a0).card) ≤ A.card
Pnq.balanced_plus_zmod : ∀ (p q n : ℕ) [inst : Fact (Nat.Prime p)] [inst_1 : Fact (Nat.Prime q)],
  p ≠ q →
    ∀ (A : Finset (ZMod (p ^ n * q))) (a0 : ℕ),
      Pqr.ZeroAt A q →
        (∀ (ℓ : ℕ), 1 ≤ ℓ → ℓ < a0 → Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ ℓ * q)) →
          1 ≤ a0 →
            a0 ≤ n →
              ¬Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ a0 * q) →
                (Pnq.levelsBeyond A a0).Nonempty →
                  (∀ (ℓ : ℕ), 1 ≤ ℓ → ℓ < a0 → ¬Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ ℓ)) →
                    (¬Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ a0) ∨
                        p = 2 ∧
                          ∀ (b : ℕ),
                            a0 < b →
                              b ≤ n →
                                (∀ g ∈ Pnq.levelsBeyond A a0, b < g) →
                                  Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ b) → Pqr.ZeroAt A (p ^ b * q)) →
                      q * p ^ (Pnq.levelsE A).card * (p ^ (Pnq.levelsBeyond A a0).card + 1) ≤ A.card

Who wrote what: the statements of gBeyond, balanced_base and balanced_plus are mine and were fixed before the proof was written; the proofs in Pnq/Balanced.lean are by a fresh instance of the model, following sections 1 to 5 of minsize-agent3/balanced-half/proof.md (another fresh instance's proof, which I have read line by line); Pnq/BalancedGroup.lean is mine. The two _zmod statements are about subsets of ZMod (p^n * q) (Finset), as sharp_lemma3_zmod is; the tree statements cover multisets. These are the two LOWER bounds only: the constructions that show the bounds are reached (Theorem C of proof.md) are not in Lean. Nobody but me has read the statements against the mathematics; Noon has said it will rebuild from the shared folder and read them.
